#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:5
#: 857229cb4e2e44c7926945bd0e9c5241
msgid "Using SITL with Webots C/C++"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:11
#: c45a351247b840c28129902ec6c31f27
msgid "`Webots <https://cyberbotics.com/>`__ is a simulator mainly used for robotics. It is easy to build many vehicles using it. ArduPilot has Rover, Quadcopter, and Tricopters examples that have been built especially for this simulator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:14
#: 13440664d37045bf832912096b0d158f
msgid "You can download Webots simulator from `www.cyberbotics.com <https://www.cyberbotics.com/#download/>`__. To run Webots just type webots in command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:18
#: 669f8a3676a84769b29d7d48d0118cc0
msgid "Running the Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:20
#: d58a3d2a5b484d8da79a9195963dc2d0
msgid "Open Webots using the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:21
#: ae735944152441cd90f7577ba893b8ee
msgid "Download and open a vehicle from the `vehicle examples folder <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/SITL/examples/Webots/worlds>`__   such as  ``webots_quadPlus.wbt``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:22
#: 765c422511544d30901cce001905557f
msgid "Compile the Robot Controller and WorldInfo physics plugin using Webots GUI by opening their respective source files (`ardupilot_SITL_QUAD.c <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/SITL/examples/Webots/controllers/ardupilot_SITL_QUAD/ardupilot_SITL_QUAD.c>`__ and `sitl_physics_env.c <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/SITL/examples/Webots/plugins/physics/sitl_physics_env/sitl_physics_env.c>`__) and running ``Build > Build``. More info about building with Webots can be found `here <https://cyberbotics.com/doc/guide/webots-built-in-editor>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:23
#: 0d236a7f6a4146779469d69174d88ae1
msgid "Press Run on Webots GUI. Now the simulator is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:24
#: bac9a5fda49a4ed88d7ce1b24c7fe603
msgid "Run ArduPilot's SITL using available scripts in the `examples folder <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/SITL/examples/Webots>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:35
#: 999c9ffdff134a47b5ee6890dd8466ed
msgid "It is important to run Webots before ArduPilot's SITL , otherwise the socket connection may not establish."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:37
#: 753abe9e9e19491cb80148ee00271cf6
msgid "As of writing, these instructions work with Webots 2021b. Newer versions may or may not work correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:40
#: a1c814bf8b01490aa08ec8ed88ea61e2
msgid "Simulation Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:42
#: 797ec8a7a4254bf48558262d04d209fc
msgid "There are two types of parameters, the first type is passed to SITL and the second is configured in Webots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:44
#: d731a5d302144c5da9c724e2f6f282e4
msgid "SITL communicates with Webots using TCP sockets, so SITL should have the same port number as Webots. Usually you don't need to change the default port 5599, but when you run multiple robots you will need to use different ports for each simulation instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:49
#: ade7d951e9f14e8eae8fc4befcb1b4cd
msgid "Advantage of Webots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:51
#: 0cdd07ff48e142be837bbf031cab869b
msgid "Controllers can be written in c, c++, python, and MatLab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-webots-cpp.rst:52
